    <statement><p><p>R is given by <m>{7x + 3y \le 49}</m>, <m>{x + 9y \le 37}</m>, <m>x \ge {1}</m> and <m>y \ge 0</m>. Give exact values (fractions or decimals).</p><p>(a) Find the vertex where <m>{7x + 3y = 49}</m> meets <m>{x + 9y = 37}</m>: ( <fillin characters="6" name="ans1"/> , <fillin characters="6" name="ans2"/> )  </p><div/><p>(b) Find the vertex where <m>{x + 9y = 37}</m> meets <m>x = {1}</m>: ( <fillin characters="6" name="ans3"/> , <fillin characters="6" name="ans4"/> )  </p><div/></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Two boundary lines meet at a vertex, so solve their equations together.</p><p>(a) Solve <m>{7x + 3y = 49}</m> and <m>{x + 9y = 37}</m> together: eliminate one letter, then substitute back. The vertex is <m>{(5.5, 3.5)}</m>.</p><p>(b) Put <m>x = {1}</m> into <m>{x + 9y = 37}</m>: <m>{1} \times {1} + {9}y = {37}</m>, so <m>y = {4}</m>. The vertex is <m>{(1, 4)}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{11}{2}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{7}{2}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>1</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>4</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>